A. Commit message:
LoongArch: Fix reserving screen info memory for above-4G firmware

B. Change summary:
The patch updates the `init_screen_info` function to correctly handle above-4G addresses for reserving screen info memory by using the `__screen_info_lfb_base` helper function. This ensures that both the lower and higher 32 bits of the address are properly managed.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/arch/loongarch/kernel/efi.c b/arch/loongarch/kernel/efi.c
index 2bf86aeda874c..de21e72759eeb 100644
--- a/arch/loongarch/kernel/efi.c
+++ b/arch/loongarch/kernel/efi.c
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@ static void __init init_screen_info(void)
 	memset(si, 0, sizeof(*si));
 	early_memunmap(si, sizeof(*si));
 
-	memblock_reserve(screen_info.lfb_base, screen_info.lfb_size);
+	memblock_reserve(__screen_info_lfb_base(&screen_info), screen_info.lfb_size);
 }
 
 void __init efi_init(void)
```